(i) The form <<ref:khtr>> of $\mathcal P$ can be expressed via the Tits form of $\mathcal P \coprod \mathcal P$ as follows:

\begin{equation*}
u_{\mathcal P}(x_0,x_1,\dots,x_t)=q_{\mathcal P \coprod \mathcal P}(x_0,x_1,\dots,x_t,x_1,\dots,x_t).
\end{equation*}

(ii) The form $u_{\mathcal P}$ is positive definite if and only if it is weakly positive definite.
The form $u_{\mathcal P}$ is nonnegative definite if and only if it is weakly nonnegative definite.
